  "about": "The explicit URL-slug map for /rankings — one human slug per dossier metric key. Hand-authored, never derived: a metric's URL is an editorial decision with a permanence obligation, not a string transformation. Total coverage, kebab-case and uniqueness are enforced by scripts/validate-rankings.mjs; lib/rankings.ts re-asserts at build. `aliases` records metric keys whose page is shared with another key carrying byte-identical data (the validator proves the identity every run): society's `literacy` and education's `literacyRate` are the same UIS indicator reaching the atlas through two pipelines, and publishing it twice would be duplicate content pretending to be two datasets.",
